{"schemaVersion":2,"dataVersion":"2026-09-03-my-gear-v2-content-1","items":[{"id":"setup-spinning","category":"rods-reels","type":"Spinning","name":"Daiwa Tatula XT + Daiwa Exceler LT","rod":{"manufacturer":{"name":"Daiwa","url":"https://daiwa.us/collections/freshwater-rods/products/tatula-xt"},"model":"Tatula XT","specifications":[{"label":"Length","value":"7'"},{"label":"Power","value":"Medium"},{"label":"Action","value":"Fast"},{"label":"Pieces","value":"2"},{"label":"Part","value":"TATULAXT702MFS"}],"links":[{"kind":"retailer","label":"Tackle Warehouse","url":"https://www.tacklewarehouse.com/Daiwa_Tatula_XT_Spinning_Rods_2-Piece/descpage-NTXT2S.html"}]},"reel":{"manufacturer":{"name":"Daiwa","url":"https://daiwa.us/collections/spin-reels/products/23-exceler-lt"},"model":"Exceler LT","specifications":[{"label":"Gear ratio","value":"6.2:1"},{"label":"Part","value":"EXELT2500D-XH"}],"links":[{"kind":"resource","label":"Maintenance video","url":"https://youtu.be/vkCUgxwUtqU?si=cZehY_eKmqr9HXdn"}]},"notes":"Primary finesse / trout / Jacob-friendly setup.\n\nCurrent line: [Sufix 832 15 lb Hi-Vis Yellow](gear://sufix-832-15) braid with [Seaguar InvizX 8 lb](gear://seaguar-invizx-8) fluorocarbon leader.\n\nBest suited to lighter presentations such as wacky worms, drop shots, Ned rigs, small jerkbaits, inline spinners, and spoons. Also preferred when easy casting, light-line control, or clear-water finesse is more important than power.\n\nSee [Rods & Reels](kb://technique-rods-reels) for general spinning-vs-baitcasting guidance and typical spinning setup recommendations."},{"id":"setup-baitcasting","category":"rods-reels","type":"Baitcasting","name":"Shimano Zodias + Shimano 22 SLX DC XT 71HG","rod":{"manufacturer":{"name":"Shimano","url":"https://fish.shimano.com/en-US/product/rods/bass/a075f000049ncdzqau_c.html"},"model":"Zodias ZDC72MHB","specifications":[{"label":"Length","value":"7'2\""},{"label":"Power","value":"Medium-heavy"},{"label":"Action","value":"Fast"}],"links":[{"kind":"retailer","label":"Amazon","url":"https://a.co/d/07UzjAvv"}]},"reel":{"manufacturer":{"name":"Shimano","url":"https://fish.shimano.com/ja-JP/product/reel/baitlurecasting/a075f00003ihbqcqay.html"},"model":"22 SLX DC XT 71HG","specifications":[{"label":"Gear ratio","value":"7.4:1"}],"links":[{"kind":"retailer","label":"JDM Tackle Heaven","url":"https://jdmtackleheaven.com/products/shimano-22-slx-dc-xt-71hg-left?_pos=1&_psq=22+SLX+DC+XT&_ss=e&_v=1.0"}]},"notes":"Primary general-purpose bass setup for heavier lures, stronger hooksets, and more accurate target casting.\n\nCurrent line: [PowerPro Super8 Slick V2 30 lb Moss Green](gear://powerpro-super8-slick-v2-30) braid with [Seaguar InvizX 12 lb](gear://seaguar-invizx-12) fluorocarbon leader.\n\nBest suited to spinnerbaits, chatterbaits, crankbaits, jigs, swimbaits, topwater, and other presentations where the spinning setup is lighter than ideal.\n\nFor the SLX DC XT, set the internal line-type dial for the line being used and adjust braking for lure weight, wind, and casting conditions. Thumb the spool at splashdown to help prevent backlash.\n\nSLX DC XT setup video: [https://youtu.be/mIcaRiMC_-k?si=-07JzU0Tlcns1zB1](https://youtu.be/mIcaRiMC_-k?si=-07JzU0Tlcns1zB1)\n\nSee [Rods & Reels](kb://technique-rods-reels) for general spinning-vs-baitcasting guidance and baitcaster setup/casting recommendations."},{"id":"setup-spincasting","category":"rods-reels","type":"Spincasting","name":"Pflueger President Spincast Combo","rod":{"manufacturer":{"name":"Pflueger","url":"https://pfluegerfishing.com/products/president-spincast-combo-1595561"},"model":"President Spincast Combo","specifications":[{"label":"Length","value":"6'6\""},{"label":"Power","value":"Medium"},{"label":"Pieces","value":"2"},{"label":"Part","value":"PRESSC-606L2CBO"}],"links":[]},"reel":{"manufacturer":{"name":"Pflueger","url":"https://pfluegerfishing.com/products/president-spincast-combo-1595561"},"model":"President Spincast Combo","specifications":[{"label":"Line weight","value":"8-14 lb"},{"label":"Gear ratio","value":"3.8:1"},{"label":"Part","value":"PRESSC-606L2CBO"}],"links":[]},"notes":"Simple, easy-to-use shore-fishing setup intended primarily for trout, kids, guests, and situations where uncomplicated casting is more important than maximum sensitivity or casting performance.\n\nA 6 lb monofilament main line is recommended for this setup. Avoid switching to braid or straight fluorocarbon main line unless actual testing shows that the reel handles it well.\n\nWell suited to PowerBait bottom rigs, bobber-and-worm rigs, and small spoons or inline spinners if they cast adequately on the reel.\n\nSee [Trout Fishing](kb://technique-trout-fishing) for general trout techniques and rigging."},{"id":"sufix-832-15","category":"line","type":"Braided","name":"Sufix 832","manufacturer":{"name":"Sufix","url":"https://www.rapala.com/us_en/832-advanced-superline?childSku=us-660-115Y"},"model":"832 Advanced Superline","specifications":[{"label":"Strength","value":"15 lb"},{"label":"Color","value":"Hi-Vis Yellow"},{"label":"Length","value":"300 yd"},{"label":"Part","value":"660-115Y"}],"links":[],"notes":"See [Fishing Line](kb://technique-fishing-line) for braid selection, leader pairing, knot, hook-set, and spooling guidance."},{"id":"powerpro-super8-slick-v2-30","category":"line","type":"Braided","name":"PowerPro Super8 Slick V2","manufacturer":{"name":"PowerPro","url":"https://fishshop.shimano.com/products/powerprosuper8slick-v2?variant=61578323624306"},"model":"Super8 Slick V2","specifications":[{"label":"Strength","value":"30 lb"},{"label":"Color","value":"Moss Green"},{"label":"Length","value":"150 yd"}],"links":[{"kind":"retailer","label":"Tackle Warehouse","url":"https://www.tacklewarehouse.com/Power_Pro_Super8Slick_V2_Braided_Line_Moss_Green/descpage-PVMG.html"}],"notes":"See [Fishing Line](kb://technique-fishing-line) for braid selection, leader pairing, knot, hook-set, and spooling guidance."},{"id":"sea